From 906426cf64e3873ac821d1d7c4cbfeabe7972f4f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kiran Maddaraki <kmaddaraki@nvidia.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 11:04:41 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] NVIDIA: SAUCE: pinctrl: paris: report no debounce support for
 EINTs without it

BugLink: https://bugs.launchpad.net/bugs/2172005

ACPI GpioInt resources ask gpiolib to set a debounce timeout, here 0,
when the GPIO is claimed.  Many EINTs on MT8901 have no debounce
hardware, the virtual GPIOs among them.  mtk_eint_set_debounce() then
fails with -EINVAL, which gpiolib reports at probe as

  gpio-N (?): Failed to set debounce-timeout 0: -22

although nothing is wrong.

Return -ENOTSUPP for an EINT that has no debounce hardware.  gpiolib
treats that as an optional setting that is not supported and stays quiet.

Signed-off-by: Kiran Maddaraki <kmaddaraki@nvidia.com>
Acked-by: Carol L Soto <csoto@nvidia.com>
Acked-by: Nirmoy Das <nirmoyd@nvidia.com>
Signed-off-by: Brad Figg <bfigg@nvidia.com>
---
 drivers/pinctrl/mediatek/pinctrl-paris.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pinctrl/mediatek/pinctrl-paris.c b/drivers/pinctrl/mediatek/pinctrl-paris.c
index 6dc4680b326e3..9091d3a971547 100644
--- a/drivers/pinctrl/mediatek/pinctrl-paris.c
+++ b/drivers/pinctrl/mediatek/pinctrl-paris.c
@@ -954,6 +954,14 @@ static int mtk_gpio_set_config(struct gpio_chip *chip, unsigned int offset,
 	    desc->eint.eint_n == EINT_NA)
 		return -ENOTSUPP;
 
+	/*
+	 * Not every EINT has debounce hardware, the virtual GPIOs among them.
+	 * Report that as unsupported so gpiolib treats the request as optional
+	 * rather than warning about an -EINVAL from the EINT driver.
+	 */
+	if (!hw->eint->pins[desc->eint.eint_n].debounce)
+		return -ENOTSUPP;
+
 	debounce = pinconf_to_config_argument(config);
 
 	return mtk_eint_set_debounce(hw->eint, desc->eint.eint_n, debounce);
